.TH OPENHAMSHACK-NB 1 "2026-10-04" "openhamshack-nb" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openhamshack-nb \- QO-100 narrowband transceiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openhamshack-nb
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
OpenHamShack QO-100 NB is a native PyQt6 desktop transceiver for the QO-100 amateur
satellite's narrowband segment (CW, SSB, FT8, FT4, PSK31/63/125, RTTY,
FreeDV and SSTV receive). A radio engine owns the SDR and does all the
signal processing; a Qt window is the whole user interface; both run in
one process on the machine at the operator's desk.
.PP
It talks to the ADALM-Pluto family of SDRs (Pluto, Pluto+, LibreSDR,
Pluto nano) over the network or USB for full transmit and receive, or to
any SoapySDR-supported receiver (RTL-SDR, Airspy, SDRplay, HackRF, \&...)
for receive only. With no hardware attached it runs against a simulated
QO-100 downlink, which is enough to explore the program, run its test
suite, or demonstrate it with no dish.
.PP
Run with no arguments to open the window. The window is the primary way
to use the program; the options below exist for testing, benchmarking,
and running the engine unattended.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run the engine without opening a window: print one status line a
second to standard output instead. Intended for tests and benchmarking,
not day-to-day operation \- there is no way to transmit from this mode
and nothing here ever keys the transmitter.
.TP
.BI \-\-device " DEVICE"
Override the configured device for this run only. One of
.BR sim ", " pluto " or " soapy .
.TP
.BI \-\-seconds " N"
Stop after
.I N
seconds instead of running until interrupted (Ctrl-C). A value of 0, the
default, means run until interrupted.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audio
Run with the null audio backend: no sound card is opened. Useful
wherever PortAudio has nothing to attach to, such as a headless build
host or a CI runner.
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log at INFO level instead of the default WARNING.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the built-in usage summary and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/openhamshack-nb/config.json
Persisted settings (frequency, mode, device, calibration). Overridden by
the
.B OHS_NB_CONF
environment variable.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/openhamshack-nb/
Logs, recordings and received SSTV images. Overridden by the
.B OHS_NB_DATA
environment variable.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OHS_NB_CONF
Path to the config file, in place of the default under
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B OHS_NB_DATA
Path to the data directory, in place of the default under
.IR ~/.local/share .
.TP
.BR OHSNB_CONF ", " OHSNB_DATA
The names these had before the OpenHamShack rename; still read when
the OHS_NB_ ones are not set.
.PP
An installation from before the rename kept its files under
.IR ~/.config/openhamshack-nb " and " ~/.local/share/openhamshack-nb .
The first start of this version moves both to the new names and leaves
a link at each old one; nothing is copied and nothing deleted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on a clean stop (Ctrl-C, SIGTERM, or \-\-seconds elapsing);
.B 1
if the engine could not start (device or audio failure);
.B 2
if run with no mode of operation and no window is available (the
message tells you to pass \-\-headless).
.SH SEE ALSO
Full engine API and design notes are installed with the source under
.IR /usr/lib/openhamshack-nb/ohsnb .
.SH AUTHOR
Brian Henderson
